{"audio": "1corinthians-09.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 204000, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 2667, "text": "1 Corinthians, Chapter Nine."}, {"start_ms": 2667, "end_ms": 4667, "text": "Am I not an apostle?"}, {"start_ms": 4667, "end_ms": 5733, "text": "am I not free?"}, {"start_ms": 5733, "end_ms": 8133, "text": "have I not seen Jesus Christ our Lord?"}, {"start_ms": 8133, "end_ms": 10133, "text": "are not ye my work in the Lord?"}, {"start_ms": 10133, "end_ms": 17733, "text": "If I be not an apostle unto others, yet doubtless I am to you: for the seal of mine apostleship are ye in the Lord."}, {"start_ms": 17733, "end_ms": 23067, "text": "Mine answer to them that do examine me is this, Have we not power to eat and to drink?"}, {"start_ms": 23067, "end_ms": 30933, "text": "Have we not power to lead about a sister, a wife, as well as other apostles, and as the brethren of the Lord, and Cephas?"}, {"start_ms": 30933, "end_ms": 34400, "text": "Or I only and Barnabas, have not we power to forbear working?"}, {"start_ms": 34400, "end_ms": 37600, "text": "Who goeth a warfare any time at his own charges?"}, {"start_ms": 37600, "end_ms": 41067, "text": "who planteth a vineyard, and eateth not of the fruit thereof?"}, {"start_ms": 41067, "end_ms": 44933, "text": "or who feedeth a flock, and eateth not of the milk of the flock?"}, {"start_ms": 44933, "end_ms": 47067, "text": "Say I these things as a man?"}, {"start_ms": 47067, "end_ms": 49467, "text": "or saith not the law the same also?"}, {"start_ms": 49467, "end_ms": 55733, "text": "For it is written in the law of Moses, Thou shalt not muzzle the mouth of the ox that treadeth out the corn."}, {"start_ms": 55733, "end_ms": 58400, "text": "Doth God take care for oxen?"}, {"start_ms": 58400, "end_ms": 60800, "text": "Or saith he it altogether for our sakes?"}, {"start_ms": 60800, "end_ms": 69200, "text": "For our sakes, no doubt, this is written: that he that ploweth should plow in hope; and that he that thresheth in hope should be partaker of his hope."}, {"start_ms": 69200, "end_ms": 75333, "text": "If we have sown unto you spiritual things, is it a great thing if we shall reap your carnal things?"}, {"start_ms": 75333, "end_ms": 79200, "text": "If others be partakers of this power over you, are not we rather?"}, {"start_ms": 79200, "end_ms": 85733, "text": "Nevertheless we have not used this power; but suffer all things, lest we should hinder the gospel of Christ."}, {"start_ms": 85733, "end_ms": 91067, "text": "Do ye not know that they which minister about holy things live of the things of the temple?"}, {"start_ms": 91067, "end_ms": 94667, "text": "and they which wait at the altar are partakers with the altar?"}, {"start_ms": 94667, "end_ms": 100000, "text": "Even so hath the Lord ordained that they which preach the gospel should live of the gospel."}, {"start_ms": 100000, "end_ms": 111333, "text": "But I have used none of these things: neither have I written these things, that it should be so done unto me: for it were better for me to die, than that any man should make my glorying void."}, {"start_ms": 111333, "end_ms": 120000, "text": "For though I preach the gospel, I have nothing to glory of: for necessity is laid upon me; yea, woe is unto me, if I preach not the gospel!"}, {"start_ms": 120000, "end_ms": 127867, "text": "For if I do this thing willingly, I have a reward: but if against my will, a dispensation of the gospel is committed unto me."}, {"start_ms": 127867, "end_ms": 129867, "text": "What is my reward then?"}, {"start_ms": 129867, "end_ms": 137733, "text": "Verily that, when I preach the gospel, I may make the gospel of Christ without charge, that I abuse not my power in the gospel."}, {"start_ms": 137733, "end_ms": 144800, "text": "For though I be free from all men, yet have I made myself servant unto all, that I might gain the more."}, {"start_ms": 144800, "end_ms": 158533, "text": "And unto the Jews I became as a Jew, that I might gain the Jews; to them that are under the law, as under the law, that I might gain them that are under the law; To them that are without law, as without law, (being not without law to God,"}, {"start_ms": 158533, "end_ms": 163067, "text": "but under the law to Christ,) that I might gain them that are without law."}, {"start_ms": 163067, "end_ms": 170933, "text": "To the weak became I as weak, that I might gain the weak: I am made all things to all men, that I might by all means save some."}, {"start_ms": 170933, "end_ms": 174933, "text": "And this I do for the gospel's sake, that I might be partaker thereof with you."}, {"start_ms": 174933, "end_ms": 180267, "text": "Know ye not that they which run in a race run all, but one receiveth the prize?"}, {"start_ms": 180267, "end_ms": 182133, "text": "So run, that ye may obtain."}, {"start_ms": 182133, "end_ms": 185733, "text": "And every man that striveth for the mastery is temperate in all things."}, {"start_ms": 185733, "end_ms": 190400, "text": "Now they do it to obtain a corruptible crown; but we an incorruptible."}, {"start_ms": 190400, "end_ms": 204000, "text": "I therefore so run, not as uncertainly; so fight I, not as one that beateth the air: But I keep under my body, and bring it into subjection: lest that by any means, when I have preached to others, I myself should be a castaway."}], "words": [{"t": "1", "s": 0, "e": 1143, "si": 0}, {"t": "Corinthians,", "s": 1143, "e": 1725, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 1785, "e": 2166, "si": 0}, {"t": "Nine.", "s": 2286, "e": 2627, "si": 0}, {"t": "Am", "s": 3536, "e": 3616, "si": 1}, {"t": "I", "s": 3738, "e": 3758, "si": 1}, {"t": "not", "s": 3819, "e": 3980, "si": 1}, {"t": "an", "s": 4021, "e": 4101, "si": 1}, {"t": "apostle?", "s": 4122, "e": 4627, "si": 1}, {"t": "am", "s": 4808, "e": 4908, "si": 2}, {"t": "I", "s": 4989, "e": 5009, "si": 2}, {"t": "not", "s": 5049, "e": 5210, "si": 2}, {"t": "free?", "s": 5291, "e": 5532, "si": 2}, {"t": "have", "s": 5753, "e": 5915, "si": 3}